[7.71, "o", "Claude\r\n"]
[8.01, "o", "  From the teams' own Kaggle writeups (private\r\n  leaderboard scores):\r\n\r\n"]
[8.13, "o", "  1. NVARC — 24.03%\r\n  • Built a large synthetic puzzle set (about\r\n    100k puzzles, 3.2M augmented samples) by\r\n"]
[8.25, "o", "    having an LLM mix puzzle descriptions and\r\n    write Python programs for the input and\r\n    output grids.\r\n"]
[8.37, "o", "  • Fine-tuned a Qwen3 model on it using the\r\n    ARChitects' 2024 recipe (per-puzzle LoRA\r\n    test-time fine-tuning, batched depth-\r\n"]
[8.49, "o", "    first-search decoding, augmentation\r\n    rescoring), ensembled with a Tiny\r\n    Recursive Model.\r\n"]
[8.61, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.01, "o", "  2. the ARChitects — 16.53%\r\n  • Switched from their 2024 autoregressive\r\n    model to a masked-diffusion LLM (LLaDA-8B)\r\n"]
[14.13, "o", "    with 2D positional encoding and per-task\r\n    test-time fine-tuning.\r\n  • Fed the model's output back in with \"soft\r\n"]
[14.25, "o", "    masking\" so it iteratively refines the\r\n    whole grid, with a second model predicting\r\n    the output grid size.\r\n"]
[14.37, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.79, "o", "  3. MindsAI & Tufa Labs — 12.64% on the\r\n  leaderboard (their writeup says 15.42%)\r\n  • Used a pruned 660M-parameter CodeT5-Large\r\n"]
[17.91, "o", "    encoder–decoder pretrained for months on\r\n    over 100M reasoning examples, about 70M of\r\n    them ARC-style.\r\n"]
[18.03, "o", "  • Nearly all the score came from test-time\r\n    adaptation: test-time training plus\r\n    Augment–Inference–Reverse–Vote over about\r\n"]
[18.15, "o", "    10k augmented inferences per task,\r\n    ensembling two checkpoints.\r\n"]
